The bloodline of Christ.
This is a record of the lineage of Jesus Christ. He is the son of David. He is also the son of Abram.
Abraham was the father of Isaac. And Isaac was the father of Jacob. And Jacob was the father of Judah and his brothers.
Yehuda was the father of Perez and Zerah. Tamar was their mother. Perez was the father of Hezron. Hezron was the father of Ram.
Ram was the father of Amminadab. Amminadab was the father of Nahshon. Nahshon was the father of Salmon.
Boaz was the father of Obed. Ruth was the mother of Obed. Obed was the father of Jesse.
Jesus was the father of King David, and David was the father of Solomon, and Solomon's mother was Uriah's wife.
Solomon was the father of Rehoboam. And Rehoboam was the father of Abijah. And Abijah was the father of Asa.
Asa was the father of Jehoshaphat. And Jehoshaphat was the father of Jehoram. And Jehoram was the father of Uzziah.
Azariah was the father of Gotham. And Gotham was the father of Ahaz. And Ahaz was the father of Hezekiah.
Structurally, Manasseh was the father of Amon, Amon was the father of Josiah.
Yosef was the father of Yekoniah and his brother. At that time, the Jewish people were forced to leave for Babylon.
After that, the family line continued. Jechoniah was the father of Shealtiel. And Shealtiel was the father of Zorubbabel.
Zerubbabel is the father of Abiud. Abiud is the father of Eliakim. Eliakim is the father of Azor.
Azor was the father of Zadok. Zadok was the father of Akim. Akim was the father of Eliud.
Alyaud was the father of Elieazar. And Elieazar was the father of Mathan. And Mathan was the father of Jacob.
Jacob was the father of Joseph; and Joseph was the husband of Mary; and Mary gave birth to Jesus, who is called Christ.
So there were 14 generations from Abram to David, then 14 generations from David until the Jews were forced to leave Babylon, then 14 generations from that time to Christ. Christ Jesus was born.
Thus Jesus Christ was born. He knew that Mary and Joseph had agreed to marry. But before they began to live together, it became clear that Mary would become pregnant. And she was conceived by the power of the Holy Spirit.
Her husband Yoshi was a faithful man. He did not want to openly mislead her. So he planned to secretly divorce her.
But as he was thinking about this, an angel of God's grace appeared to him in a dream. And the angel said to him, "Joseph, son of David, do not fear to take Mary as your wife. The child within her is from the Holy Spirit."
He will be born a son. You must name him Jesus. This is because he will save his people from their sins.
All of this happened so that what God had said would happen. He said this through the Apostle,
The girl will give birth to a son. She will give birth to a son, and his name will be called Emmanuel. (Isaiah 7:14) The name Emmanuel means "God with us."
Joseph awoke, and did what the angel of the Lord commanded him. And he took Mary as wife.
But he did not love her, even after she gave birth to a child. And Joseph gave him the name Jesus.
The wise men visit Jesus.
Jesus was born in Bethlehem, in Judea. This happened while Herod was king of Judea. After Jesus was born, wise men from the east came to Jerusalem.
They asked, "Where is the child who was born to be king of the Jews? For we saw his star when it rose and have come to worship him."
When King Herod heard this, he was deeply disturbed, and all in Jerusalem were terrified.
Therefore Herod called together all the chief priests of the people, and the teachers who were respected for their knowledge of the law. He asked them the exact location where the Messiah was to be born.
"In Bethlehem in the hand of the Lord," they answered. "This is what the prophet wrote: 'He said:'"
"But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah, though you are small among the clans of Judah, out of you will come one who will rule Israel, whose origins are from of old, from ancient times." (Micah 5:2)
So Herodi informed the secret agents of the ongoing research. He learned from them precisely the time of the star's emergence.
Send them to Bethlehem. And he said, "Go! Search diligently for the child. And when you find him, inform me. Then I will go and worship him also."
After the wise men had heard the king, they went on their way. The star that they had seen in the east went before them, and at last stood still over the place where the child was.
When they saw the star, they were filled with joy.
The wise men came to the house. They saw the child with his mother Mary. They saluted him and worshipped him. Then they opened their treasures, and offered him gold, frankincense and myrrh.
But God sent them a message in a dream, telling them not to return to Herod's territory. So they returned to their own country by another route. Thus, Jesus's family fled to Egypt.
When the wise gentlemen departed, a dream came upon Joseph. In the dream, a multitude of the mercy of God appeared to him. And the multitude said to him, "Arise! Lift up the child and his mother and flee into Egypt and remain there until I tell you to return. Herod will be waiting for the child, and he wants to kill him."
Joseph awoke. During the night, he left with the child and his mother Mary Egypt.
They remained there until King Herod died. Thus, the word of the Lord spoken by the prophet was fulfilled: "I called my son out of Egypt." (Hosea 11:1)
Herod realized that the men had deceived him, for in his intense rage he gave orders to massacre all the male children in Bethlehem and its vicinity who were two years old or less. This was in accordance with the time he had ascertained from the men when the star appeared to them.
With this, the words of a prophet from Yarmouk became true. He had said:
A voice is heard in Ramah, a voice of weeping and great mourning. Rachel weeps for her children; she refuses to be comforted, because they are gone. (Job 31:15) The family of Christ returns to Nazareth.
After Herod died, Joseph had a dream while he was living in Egypt. And in the dream, a messenger appeared to him from God's mercy.
The narrator said: "Awaken! Take the child and his mother, and depart for the land of Israel. For he who was attempting to kill shall be killed."
And Joseph awoke, and took the child and his mother Mary, and returned to the land of Israel.
But then he heard that Archelaus was king of Judea. Archelaus was ruling in place of his father Herod. This made Joseph afraid to go there. Joseph was reminded in a dream, so he returned to the land of Galilea.
And he lived there in a city called Nazareth. So what the apostles said about Jesus was true. She said, "He will be called Nazareth."
John the Baptist is preparing the way.
In those days John the Baptist came and preached in the wilderness of Judea.
He said, "Rise from your errors! For the kingdom in heaven is near."
John is the one about whom the Lord Jesus spoke. And He said, "He is the one about whom it is written: 'Behold, I send My messenger before Your face, who will prepare Your way before You.' " (Malachi 3:1,2)
John's clothing was made of donkey fur. He owned a leather string around his depth. His food was nerves and external bees.
Bring out the people from Jerusalem and all of Judaea, and arrive from all the surrounding area of the Jordan River.
When they confessed that they had surrendered, John baptized them in the Jordan.
John saw many Pharisees and Sadducees coming to his place of purification. He said to them, "You are like a follower of the tradition of tradition! Who told you to flee from the arrival of God's wrath?"
Produce a fruit showing that you have strayed from your path.
Do not suppose that you can say to yourselves, 'Abram is our father.' I say to you, God can raise up children to Abraham even from these stones.
The root of the tree is wide and expansive. Every tree that does not bear good fruit will be cut down and thrown into the fire.
I baptize you with water, and I call you to repent of your sins. But after me will come one mightier than I, whose sandals I am not worthy to carry. He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit and with fire.
The hand of the deliverer is in his hand to clean the barley from the discharge area. He will gather his grain in the storehouse. But he will burn the grain with the unquenchable fire. "Jesus is cleansing"
Jesus came from Galilee to the Jordan River, desiring to be cleansed by John.
But Johannes tried to stop him. And he said to Isa: "I need to be cleansed of you, so why are you coming to me?"
Jesus answered, "Let this be now. For it is meet to do this. For he does the will of God the Great." Then John agreed also.
When Jesus was baptized, he rose from the water. At that moment, the heavens were opened. And Jesus saw the Spirit of God descend on him like a dove.
A voice from heaven said, "This is my son, whom I love; I am well pleased with him."
Jesus is being crucified.
Jesus, led by the Holy Spirit, was taken into the wilderness, where he was tempted by the devil.
After 40 days and 40 nights of not eating, Jesus became disabled by hunger.
The tester came to him and said, "If you are the Son of God, command these stones to become bread."
Jesus answered, "It is written, 'Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceeds from the mouth of God.'" (Deuteronomy 8:3)
Then the devil took Jesus to the holy city, and placed him on the highest point of a church building.
"If you are a son of your Lord," he said, "come down. And it is written: 'Your Lord will command that you hand over yourselves to Him, and you will be raised up by your own hands. Let us cling to a stone.'" (Surah 91:11, 12)
Jesus answered him, saying, "It is written, 'You shall not tempt the Lord your God.'" (Deuteronomy 6:16)
Finally, the devil took Jesus to a very high mountain. And he showed him all the kingdoms of the world and their glory.
"If you surrender and worship me," he said, "I will give you all of this."
Jesus said to him: "Depart from me, Satan! For it is written: 'You shall worship the Lord your God, and Him only you shall serve.'" (Deuteronomy 6:13)
Then the devil left Jesus, and they believed and attended to him. Jesus began to teach.
John was thrown into prison. When Jesus heard about this, he returned to Galilee.
Jesus of Nazareth went to live in the town of Capernaum by the lake, in the region of Zebulun and Naphtali.
With this, what the prophet Joshua said became true. He said:
Land of Zebulun! Land of Naphtali! Galilee, where non-Jewish people live! Land located on the Mediterranean Sea! Region located to the east of the Jordan River!
People who are now living in darkness will see a great light. They are now living in a very dark land. But light will shine on them. (Isaiah 9:1, 2)
From that time, Jesus began to preach. "Repent of your sins!" he said. "The Kingdom of Heaven is at hand." Jesus chooses the first teachers
One day, Jesus was walking by the Sea of Galilee. There he saw two brothers. They were Simon Peter and his brother Andrew. They were casting a net into the lake. They were fishers by trade.
"I am dying, follow me," said Jesus. "I will make you fishers of men."
Put out their nets immediately and follow him.
And so he saw that there were two other brothers. They were James, son of Zebedee, and his brother John. They were in a boat with their father Zebedee. While they were preparing the net, Jesus called them.
Come out of the boat immediately, with their father, and follow Jesus. Jesus heals the sick.
Jesus was sent to all parts of Galilee. He was teaching in the schools. He was announcing good news about the kingdom of God. He was healing every disease and sickness that the people suffered from.
People were told about him all over Syria. And people brought to him everyone who was sick with a different disease. And some of them were suffering from severe pain, and others were controlled by demons, and others were shaking violently, and others could not move at all. And Jesus healed them all.
A great number of people followed him. Some came from Galilee, from the region known as the Decapolis, from Jerusalem and Judea. Others came from the region located across the Jordan River.
Jesus gives wishes.
Jesus saw the crowds. He went up into a mountain, and when he had sat down, his disciples came to him.
Then he began to teach them. He said:
The hearing which is deserved for those who work with a life which is deserved. The angel of the heavens belongs to them.
The flat heavens are being subdued upon death.
Blessed is the hearing of those who were not, for it is no cause for pride. They shall be given the earth of the heavens.
Hearing is for those who love and fear goodness. So they will be granted.
Peace be upon the righteous. Peace will be given.
Peace be upon those who have prayed with their hearts. They shall see God.
Hearing is for those who teach peace, and they will be called children of God.
Blessed are they that suffer persecution for righteousness' sake: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.
You are magnified when people mock and harm you because of me. You are also magnified when they tell you bad news of any kind because of me.
Be happy and joyful. For your reward in heaven is great. In the same way, people hurt the messengers who lived in the past. Salt and light.
You are the salt of the earth. But suppose the salt loses its taste. How can it be made salty again? It is no longer good for anything. It will be thrown out and trampled under people's feet.
You are the light of the world. No one lights a lamp and puts it under a basket, but rather puts it on a lampstand, so that those who come in may see the light.
Also, people don't light a lamp and put it under a bowl. Instead, they put it on its stand. Then the light shines for everyone in the house.
Jesus gives complete meaning to the law.
Do not think that I came to delete what was mentioned in the law or in the messenger. I did not come to do that. Rather, I came to present a complete meaning of what was mentioned.
What I am about to tell you now is a reality. Heaven and earth will pass away before even a single letter of the Law vanishes. Not the smallest detail of the Scriptures of the Pen will vanish from the Law until everything is completed.
Do not break any of the small commandments, and do not teach others to break them. For if you do, you will be called the least important people in the Kingdom of Heaven. But do and teach these commandments. And you will be called important in the Kingdom of Heaven.
Here is what I tell you: you must be more righteous than the Pharisees and the teachers of the law. If you are not, you will not enter the kingdom of heaven. Kill
You have heard what he said to the people who lived in a time long ago. And they were told, "You shall not kill. (Brothers 20:13) And whoever kills will be punished for it."
But here is what I tell you: Don't be angry with your brother. Whoever is angry with his brother will be brought to judgment. Again, whoever says to his brother, 'You are a fool!' will be in danger of the council. But whoever says, 'You moron!' will be in danger of the fire of hell.
Start by displaying your gift on the aisle, then remember that your brother has something against you.
Keep your gift in front of the tablets. First, go and join your brother and forget him. Then return and present your gift.
If someone is claiming a right against you and is bringing a case against you in court, act quickly. Deal with it while you are with him on his way. If you do not do that, the judge may rule against you, then the official may act against you, and you may be detained in prison.
What I am going to tell you is the truth. You will not leave until you pay the last penny! The commission
You have heard that he said, "Do not commit adultery" (Exodus 20:14)
But I say to you: Do not set your heart on anything evil. For anyone who sets his heart on evil, has already committed it in his heart.
If your right eye causes you to sin, tear it out and throw it away. For the eye is only a part of the body, and it is better to lose it than to lose the whole body and be thrown into hell.
If your hand causes you to sin, cut it off and forget about it. For your hand is a part of your body, and it is better to lose it than to lose your whole body in hell. Divorce.
He said, "When a man separates from his wife, if he separates, he must give her a certificate of separation." (Deuteronomy 24:1)
But here is what I tell you: Whoever divorces his wife causes her to commit adultery; and whoever marries a divorced woman commits adultery. A man can divorce his wife only if she has not believed in him. Beliefs
Again, I heard what had been proclaimed to your people long ago. It was described to them: "Do not break the promises that you make to God, and keep the vows that you have promised to Him."
But here's what I'm telling you: Do not make any vows of this kind at all. Do not make them in the name of heaven. That is God's throne.
Do not make them in the name of the Earth. That is the bed for the foot of God. Do not make them in the name of Jerusalem. That is the city that the great King owns.
And do not be completed, for you have learned the names of your head. So it is not enough for any of you for his days or for his blacks.
Keep "yes" meaning "yes", and keep "no" meaning "no". Anything beyond that comes from the devil. Be merciful to the brethren.
You have heard that it was said, "An eye for an eye, and a tooth for a tooth." (Matthew 5:38; Luke 6:38; John 7:38)
But here's what I tell you: Don't fight a bad person. "If someone strikes you on the right cheek, offer your left cheek to that person as well."
If someone takes your clothes from you in court, then let them also take your clothes.
If someone forces you to go a mile, go with them two miles.
Give to anyone who asks something from you. Do not deny someone who wishes to borrow from you. Love your enemies.
You have heard that it was said, "Love your neighbor and hate your enemy." (Matthew 5:43, slightly paraphrased for clarity as the original Greek is often interpreted this way).
But here is what I tell you: Love your enemies. Pray for those who hurt you.
They will be your father's children, who are in heaven. "He causes his sun to rise on the evil and the good, and sends rain on the righteous and the unrighteous." He shows mercy to the wicked, those who work for good and those who do not."
If you love those who love you, what reward will you get? Even tax collectors do that.
If you only give gifts to your family, what more are you doing than others? Even those who are considered to be unbelievers do that.
Therefore, you should be perfected, just as the one who is perfected is in the heavens.
Being kind to needy people.
Work discreetly and do not do "good works" before people. Do not do them so that you may be seen by others. If you do this, it will be deserved of you by your Father in the heavens.
When you give to those in need, let it not be done in secret, but rather openly, as if you were proclaiming it with the sword of the true believer. And do not be like those who only show that they are pious. They announce what they do in the two churches and on the streets. They want to be respected by others. What I am going to tell you now is the truth. They have received the full reward.
When you give to those who need, do not let your left hand know what your right hand is doing.
Your donation will be done secretly. Your father will reward you. He sees what you do secretly. Prayer.
When you pray, be not as the hypocrites, for they love to pray standing in the synagogues and at the corners of the streets, that they may be seen by men. Woe to you scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites, for you are like whitewashed tombs, which outwardly appear beautiful, but within are full of dead men's bones and all uncleanness. Even so, on the outside you appear righteous to men, but within you are full of hypocrisy and lawlessness. Blind Pharisee, first clean the inside of the cup and of the platter, that the outside of them may be clean also. Woe to you scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites, for you pay tithe of mint and anise and cumin, but have omitted the weightier matters of the law, judgment, mercy, and faith. These you ought to have done, without leaving the others undone. You blind guides, who strain out a gnat and swallow a camel! Woe to you scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites, for you are like unseen tombs, which men walk over without knowing it. You Pharisees and experts in the law, hypocrites, you build tombs for the prophets and decorate the tombs of the righteous. And you say, 'If we had lived in the days of our ancestors, we would not have participated with them in shedding the blood of the prophets.' By saying this, you declare yourselves to be the righteous children of those who murdered the prophets. You serpents, you offspring of vipers, how will you escape being condemned to hell? Therefore, I tell you, every careless word you utter will be held against you on the day of judgment. For by your words you will be acquitted, and by your words you will be condemned. Then some of the legal experts (scribes) said to him, 'Teacher, we want to see a sign from you.' But he answered them, 'An evil and adulterous generation seeks for a sign, but no sign will be given to it, except the sign of the prophet Jonah.' And he said to them, 'When the evening comes, you say, "It will be fair weather, for the sky is red," and in the morning, "It will be stormy today, for the sky is red and lowering."' Hypocrites! You know how to interpret the appearance of the sky, but you do not know how to interpret the signs of the times. And he said to the crowds, 'When you see a cloud rising in the west, you immediately say, "A rainstorm is coming," and it does. And when you see the south wind blow, you say, "A hot day is coming," and it does. Hypocrites! You know how to interpret the earth and the sky, but you do not know how to interpret the present time. And as he was sitting on the Mount of Olives, his disciples came to him privately, saying, "Tell us, when will these things be, and what will be the sign of your coming and of the end of the age?" And Jesus answered them, saying, "Take heed that no one deceives you, for many will come in my name, saying, "I am the Christ," and they will deceive many. And you will hear of wars and rumors of wars; see that you are not troubled, for these things must come to pass, but the end is not yet. For nation will rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom; and there will be earthquakes in various places, and there will be famines and troubles; and there will be fearful sights and great signs from heaven. But before all these things, they will lay their hands on you and will persecute you, delivering you to synagogues and prisons, bringing you before kings and governors for my name's sake. And it will lead to your testimony. You will be hated by all for my name's sake, but he who end
When you pray, go into your room. Close the door and pray to your father, who cannot be seen. He will reward you. Your father sees what is done in secret.
When you pray, do not babble on like the unbelievers do. For they think that they will be heard because of their much speaking.
Do not be like them. Your ruler knows what you need before you ask him.
This is how you should pray. "Our Father who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name."
May your kingdom come. May what you desire to happen on earth happen as it happens in the heavens.
Give us this day our daily bread.
Forgive us our trespasses, as we forgive those who trespass against us.
Deliver us from evil. And keep us from the ladder when we are pulled. And keep us from evil.
Prepare for the things that you will consider permissible in your affairs. And if you have things that you will consider permissible in your affairs, then it will not be considered permissible for you, you who believe in God and the Last Day.
But if you do not forgive people their mistakes, your mistakes will not be forgiven by your Lord. Fasting.
When you go without eating, you do not look as sad as someone who only shows that they are pious. They show their sad faces. They want to show people that they are fasting. What I will tell you is true. They have received the full reward.
But when you go out without eating, put olive oil on your head. Wash your face.
So they do not know that you are connecting. Only your father, who cannot be seen, will know this. He will reward you. Your father sees what is done secretly. Keep the money in the sky.
Do not bury your wealth in the ground. For neither the black nor the dead can destroy it, nor can the thief steal it.
Instead, lay up your treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust destroys, and where thieves do not break in or steal.
Your heart will be where your money is.
The eye is like a lamp for the body. If your eye is good, your whole body will be illuminated.
But suppose your eyes are weak. Then your whole body will be filled with darkness. And if the light within you is darkness, then it is a very great darkness!
No one can serve two masters at the same time. Either he will hate one and love the other, or he will be devoted to one and despise the other. You cannot serve both God and Money. Do not worry.
Let me assure you: do not be anxious. Do not be anxious about your life, and what you will get for food or drink. And do not be anxious about your body, and what you will get for clothing. Is there more to life than eating? Are there things more important for the body than clothing?
Look at the birds in the sky. They do not sow or gather into barns. Yet your heavenly Father feeds them. Are you not much more valuable than they?
Can you add one hour to your life by worrying?
And when they lived long upon the traces, look how the forbidden flower sprouts. It did not take action or reach out to the traces.
But here is what I will tell you: Solomon, in all his glory, was not arrayed like one of those flowers.
If this is how God clothes the grassy tree, why wouldn't He clothe you even better? After all, the grassy tree exists only for today, but tomorrow it is thrown into the fire. And your mind is so weak!
So do not worry. Do not say, "What shall we eat?" or "What shall we drink?" or "What shall we wear?"
People who are in undeserved worship want all those things. And the Father who is in heaven knows that you need them.
But make the Kingdom of God a priority. Do what God wants you to do. Then he will get it all too.
Therefore, do not worry about tomorrow. Tomorrow will worry about itself. Each day has enough worries of its own.
Be fair when you judge others.
Do not judge people, for you will not be judged yourselves.
You will be judged as you judge others. They will be measured as you measure others.
You look at the sawdust in your friend's eye, but you don't notice the log in your own eye.
How can you say to your friend, "I will remove a piece of wood ash from your eye"? How can you say this while there is a piece of wood in your eye?
You are the deceiver! First, take the wooden beam out of your own eye, and then you will see clearly to remove the wooden splinter from your friend's eye.
Do not give what is sacred to dogs. Do not throw your pearls before swine. If you do, they may trample them under their feet, and then turn and tear you to pieces. Ask, seek, knock
Ask, and it will be given to you. Seek, and you will find. Knock, and the door will be opened for you.
Whoever asks will be answered. Whoever seeks will find. The door will be opened for whoever knocks.
If your son asks for bread, which of you will give him a stone?
Or suppose he orders fish. Which of you would pass on to him a turtle?
Even if you are bad, you know how to give good things to your children. How much more, then, will your heavenly Father give to those who ask Him!
In everything, do to others what you would have them do to you. This is what was said in the law and the apostles. The great and small door.
Enter the kingdom of God through the narrow gate. For the gate is wide and the way is easy that leads to destruction and death. Many people go by that road.
But the door is small and the path is narrow, leading to life. Few people find this path. A tree and its branches
You are being warned about false apostles. They come to you appearing as genuine messengers, but inwardly they are ravenous wolves.
You can tell if they're real by what they do. "Do people pick follicles from trees? Do they pick fruits from love?"
Likewise, every good tree produces good fruit. But a bad tree produces bad fruit.
A good tree does not produce bad fruit, and a bad tree does not produce good fruit.
Every tree that does not bear good fruit is cut down and thrown into the fire.
You can distinguish every tree by its fruits.
Not everyone who says to me, 'Lord, Lord,' will enter the kingdom of heaven, but only he who does the will of my Father in heaven.
They will say to me very much on that day: "Our Lord! Our Lord! We were not informed in Your name? We did not cast out demons in Your name? We did not perform much of the magic in Your name?"
Then I will clearly inform them: "I do not know you, stay away from me, which of you is good committed in him!" The wise builders and those who are built with abortion.
Therefore, everyone who hears my words and acts on them will be like the wise man who built his house on the rock.
Rain falls. The water rises. The wind blows and breathes on this house. But it does not collapse. It is built on the rock.
But everyone who hears my words and does not apply them is like a wise man. He builds his house on the sand.
Rain falls. The water rises. Winds blow and breathe upon this house. Then it collapses with a great explosion.
Jesus completed saying all these things. And the people were amazed at his teaching.
He taught in the manner of one who possessed authority. He did not speak like their law professors.
Jesus heals a man who was sick with a skin disease.
Jesus came down from the mountain. A large crowd followed him.
A man who was sick with a skin disease came and knelt before Jesus. "Master," he said, "if you are willing to make me clean, it is all the same to me."
Jesus took his hand and connected with the man. "I am willing to do this," he said. "Be clean!" As soon as he said it, the man returned, healed of his skin disease.
Jesus said to him, "Do not tell this to anyone, but go, show yourself to the priest, and make the offering that Moses commanded. This will be a testimony for them." A Roman Centurion Believes
When Jesus entered Capernaum, a Roman centurion came to him, asking for his help.
"Sir," he said, "my servant suffers at home and cannot move. He suffers greatly."
Jesus said, "I will go and heal him."
The captain answered, "Lord, I am not worthy to have you come into my house. But just say the word, and my servant will be healed.
I myself am a man who is being recovered for him. And he has soldiers who obey my orders. I say to one, "Go," and he goes. I say to another, "Crown," and he crowns. I say to my slaves, "Do this," and they do it.
When Jesus heard this, he smiled. And he said to those who followed him, "What I am going to tell you is the truth. In Israel, I have not found anyone who has such a strong belief as this."
I tell you, many people will come from the east and the west, and they will be seated at the feast in the kingdom of heaven. And they will be seated with Abraham and Isaac and Jacob.
But as for those who think they belong to the kingdom, they will end up outside in the darkness, where there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.
Jesus said to the Roman officer, "Go, and as you believed, so let it be done for you." And his servant was healed at that moment. Jesus heals many people.
When Jesus came to Peter's house, he saw Peter's wife. She was lying in bed and was sick with a fever.
Jesus took her hand, and her fever left her. And she arose and began to help him.
When the night came, many people who were possessed by demons were brought to Jesus; He cast them out with a word, and healed all who were sick.
